{"dossier":"D09","entry_points":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::early_cpu_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::init_cpu_devs","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::identify_cpu","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::identify_boot_cpu","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::identify_secondary_cpu","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology_common.c::cpu_parse_topology"],"text":"Early populates vendor table; per-CPU discovers, parses topology, merges SMP caps narrowing features and broadening bugs; boot finishes cache; secondary reuses once."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::syscall_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::wrmsrq_cstar","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::idt_syscall_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::enable_sep_cpu"],"text":"Publishes selectors in star then programs 64-bit entry, compat behavior, gates and flag mask; 32-bit enable publishes gate entry."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/intel.c::mce_intel_feature_init"],"text":"Applies model quirks then corrected and local enablement, finishing with memory-controller handling."}],"exports":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c::topology_get_logical_id","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::print_cpu_info","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::setup_clearcpuid","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/common.c::setup_setcpuid"],"text":"Maps APIC id to dense index with range checks; reports CPU info preferring kernel table; clear/set handlers succeed trivially."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::mcheck_cpu_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/p5.c::intel_p5_mcheck_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/winchip.c::winchip_mcheck_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/intel.c::intel_init_cmci","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/intel.c::intel_init_lmce","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/intel.c::lmce_supported","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::__mcheck_cpu_setup_timer"],"text":"Per-CPU MCE covers legacy, caps, pool, timer, generic and vendor setup; CMCI falls back to polling, LMCE needs locked control."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/amd.c::mce_amd_feature_init"],"text":"AMD setup applies quirks, enables scalable vectors, and configures thresholding where hardware reports usable entries."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/threshold.c::mce_get_apei_thr_limit","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/threshold.c::mce_inherit_storm","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/internal.h::mce_inherit_storm","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/internal.h::cmci_storm_begin"],"text":"Returns stored firmware threshold limit; storm inheritance assumes worst-case errors at current tick, empty when disabled."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/rdrand.c::x86_init_rdrand"],"text":"Samples hardware RNG 8 times requiring 5 changes and no failure, else withdraws both caps and reports unreliability."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/tsx.c::tsx_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/tsx.c::tsx_ap_init"],"text":"Boot policy revokes dev mode, handles always-abort, resolves auto from bug presence, enables or disables; APs mirror decision."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/genpool.c::mce_gen_pool_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/genpool.c::mce_gen_pool_create"],"text":"Pool creation is idempotent, sizes from node order and max of minimum versus per-CPU reservation, cleaning partial state."}],"extracts":["5a6452bd7b10dea2544daef9dd6ded96d7fbbb3be394766f6aa5cf9e1459e7c0","6bc7d37144b46a0574532ccbe041b7f0e53a6787b4b8a01a3ed3969a0881a600"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology_common.c::parse_legacy","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c::topology_get_logical_id","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.h::topo_domain_mask"],"text":"Undersized firmware shift collapses thread and core levels with warning; lookup fails with negative errors; mask needs defined widths."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::__mcheck_cpu_cap_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::__mcheck_cpu_init_prepare_banks","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::mce_zhaoxin_feature_init"],"text":"Excess banks clamp with warning; retained prior-reset errors log without dispatch; named models mute high bank to avoid VM panics."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/c